# engines/modules/default.list -- the module list proposed for an FM-1
# firmware image (FM1_MODULES=default; engines/modules/catalogue.mk;
# DEVELOPERS.md, "Choosing the modules"). One id or more a line; '#' starts
# a comment. Proposed 2026-10-06, for the owner to settle.
#
# The budget: the app area up to 0xD9000 in FM-1+VA's layout is 852 KiB
# (872,448 B); 200 KiB of it is reserved for JieLi's libraries and the
# device's platform code [inferred: fm1-nes's whole AC79 app with USB alone
# is 129,392 B, with USB audio 201,296 B, reported], which leaves 667,648 B
# for the objects of the JieLi check at -Oz. Every module together measures
# 845,716 B there (127 %), so this list leaves out the three largest costs
# that have a smaller sibling in the list [verified: tools/jieli/compile-check.sh,
# 2026-10-06, FM1_MODULES=all; the list's own run is in DEVELOPERS.md]:
#
#   comet        Comet Kit, 140,024 B even with its cymbals in 8-bit mu-law
#                (Crater Kit and Drums stay)
#   macro-heavy  Macro Heavy, 60,747 B of Plaits' heavier models beyond
#                what Macro shares with it (Macro stays)
#   test-sine test-gain test-ext   the test modules, 2,111 B
#
# GPL modules (acid-bass, crater, drawbar, trio, phase-bend, acid-gen) are
# listed: the GPL switch decides whether a build has them (FM1_GPL_MODS=0
# drops them, as the image that may be shared must).

# Sound engines
macro shapes sixop dx7 sw-sophie drums
acid-bass crater drawbar trio phase-bend

# Audio effects
plate ensemble diffuse sw-psxverb crush fold drive echo filter comb comp
limit djfilter tilt sat isolator eq room hall gate squash shaper warble repeat

# MIDI effects
arp acid-gen

# Modulation kinds
lfo env chance function bounce register coin divide burst slew quantize
compare logic calc mix resonator
